# No Fast Models

Never select, spawn, or route work to a model whose id or label includes `fast` — for the main agent, Task/subagents, or any other model picker.

## Do not use

- Any model with `fast` in the name (e.g. `composer-2.5-fast`, `grok-4.7-high-fast`)
- Defaulting to a `*-fast` model for "simple" or "quick" subtasks

## Allowed

- Non-`fast` models are fine, including flash / lite / mini / nano variants when those are what you want

## Do instead

- Use the non-`fast` counterpart (e.g. `composer-2.5`, not `composer-2.5-fast`; `grok-4.7-high`, not `grok-4.7-high-fast`)
- If the user asks for a `*-fast` model, refuse and use the non-fast equivalent
